@startuml
title Server Shutdown - Redis-like Server

' The order of a stop (SDD 11.2, 14.3; UC-017). serve() races the accept
' loop, housekeeping and the wait for a signal; sessions are outside the race
' and are drained through the listener's counting scope afterwards.
' Thread hops are in the connection feature's
' sequence_threads_request_and_shutdown.puml; this one shows the steps.

actor Operator
participant "serve()\n(race)" as Serve
participant "Listener\n(accept loop,\ncounting scope)" as Listener
participant "Sessions" as Sessions
participant "RedisServer::run()" as Run
participant "Keyspace\n(Executor)" as KS
participant "SnapshotManager" as Snap
participant "AppendOnlyFile\n(--appendonly)" as Aof
participant "main()" as Main

== A signal, or a failure, ends the race ==
Operator -> Serve : SIGINT or SIGTERM
Serve -> Serve : log "Received SIGTERM, shutting down"
note over Serve
  The first of the accept loop, housekeeping and the signal
  to finish cancels the other two through the stop token.
  A failed accept loop or housekeeping (FailFast) ends the server
  the same way, with its error recorded.
end note

== Stop accepting, drain sessions ==
Serve -> Listener : stop(): close the acceptor,\ncancel the sessions via the scope's stop token
Listener -> Sessions : stop token
Sessions -> Sessions : each session unwinds;\nunsent replies are dropped
Serve -> Listener : co_await drained()
Listener --> Serve : every session has finished
Serve -> Serve : io.stop()

== Final steps, after the I/O threads have joined ==
Serve --> Run : event loop returns
alt an I/O thread failed
  Run --> Main : ServerError (WorkerFailed)
else
  Run -> KS : stop(): wait for the executing batch
  Run -> Snap : cancel_background_save()
  note right of Snap
    A running BGSAVE would make the final save fail
    ("already in progress"), and its snapshot
    predates the latest writes.
  end note
  opt --appendonly
    Run -> Aof : cancel_rewrite()
    Run -> Aof : close(): flush, sync, release the lock
  end
  Run -> Snap : save(db): atomic replacement of --dump
  alt saved
    Run -> Run : log "Redis is now ready to exit, bye bye..."
    Run --> Main : ok
    Main --> Operator : exit status 0
  else save failed
    Run --> Main : ServerError (FinalSaveFailed)
    Main -> Main : log critical "final snapshot failed: <reason>"
    Main --> Operator : exit status non-zero (EXIT_FAILURE),\nprevious snapshot left in place
  end
end

@enduml
